=== scope
function f IN => q
=== text
%LANGUAGE FBD
%NETWORK
f(IN := i, OUT => k, q => m);
=== refused
network-plain-st the function box f wires OUT => at a root

#### out-target-on-a-program — a program declares no OUT: the variable lands past its names, or on its first output
=== scope
program p a => q1
=== text
%LANGUAGE FBD
%NETWORK
p(a := a, OUT => k);
=== refused
network-plain-st declares no output OUT

