#### old-form-return — RETURN := a; is no network text
=== text
%LANGUAGE LD
%NETWORK
RETURN := a;
=== refused
network-plain-st a jump or a return is a target of an ASSIGN

#### old-form-nested-coil — (y := a) in a value is no network text
=== text
%LANGUAGE LD
%NETWORK
ASSIGN((y := a) AND b, Q => x);
=== refused
network-plain-st a coil inside a value is ASSIGN(value, Q => y)

#### old-form-not — NOT a is no network text: a negation is INVERT(a)
=== text
%LANGUAGE LD
%NETWORK
ASSIGN(b AND NOT a, Q => x);
=== refused
network-plain-st a mark is a function around a value

